Protein Name: GFP-like non-fluorescent chromoprotein (NFCP)
Organism: Discosoma sp. (Coral)
UniProt Accession ID: Q95W85
Protein Function: This protein belongs to the GFP-like fluorescent protein family. Unlike green fluorescent protein (GFP), this chromoprotein does not show fluorescence but contains a chromophore responsible for its visible coloration. GFP-like chromoproteins are widely studied for understanding protein structure, chromophore formation, and their applications in biotechnology and molecular imaging.
Cellular Location: Cytoplasm.
